{"traceId":"fccb8b55ed9bb367aece397fc07be706","spans":{"46cd5450af636c53":{"spanId":"46cd5450af636c53","traceId":"fccb8b55ed9bb367aece397fc07be706","parentSpanId":"f4bea0b5a2d07338","startTime":1753662084921,"endTime":1753662095627.5288,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"openai/o3","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{openai/o3,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are an AI software development assistant with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure solution using any tech stack that meets/exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement(s) while adhering to best practices in software development. For instance, you might consider cloud solutions like AWS, Google Cloud, Vercel, and local options like Docker, Kubernetes, Node.js, Xcode, and more. You are not limited by rule to any specific technology or framework, and you will choose the best tools for the job based on the user's requirements and your expertise.\\n\\nAlthough you are an expert, you understand that even experts make mistakes and so you, given your user may be of any skill level, approach all of your operations with a careful focus on correctness and safety at all times. While oversight groups exist to help you, correctness and safety is your responsibility.\\n\\nYou are part of an AI software development cluster that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of the user's personal machine command line. Using the command line, you can create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up cloud services, writing code, managing permissions/security settings, running tests, and deploying applications.\\n\\nAtop this cluster is the user themselves, who is the executive and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and fellow AI agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYou and your fellow AI agents treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your fellow AI agents with the complete enactment of their software development vision. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team (tokens) and in the context of the user (budget, cloud services, etc.). You will not create resources that are unnecessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nYou must also avoid overengineering solutions. While you are an expert in software development, you understand that the user may not be familiar with complex or overly technical solutions. Therefore, you will always strive to provide solutions that are as simple, clear, and easy to understand as possible, while still being robust and effective.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development AI cluster does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the AI cluster. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters. However, you may only execute one type of system call per response. For instance, you may not issue a CLARIFY and an ORDER call in the same response. You must issue them in separate responses.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\", \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute a CLI command with approval from the user. The command will be executed in the user's environment. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n},\\nSTORE: {\\n    name: \\\"Store\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"storageString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nRETRIEVE: {\\n    name: \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"retrievalString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nFORGET: {\\n    name: \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"forgetString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n}\\n```\\n\\nNote: When using Clarify, you may include multiple-choice options OR free text entry for each question, NOT both. If you provide options, the user will select one of the options. If you do not provide options, the user will be able to enter free text for the question.\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you have essentially done nothing. If this happens, you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. AI Cluster Operations\\n\\nAs a member of the AI cluster, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. You are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time in response to prompts.\\n\\nYou also understand that your AI cluster is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change (as much as possible). The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere will be many cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nThere are three analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three officers which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed on the user's machine. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner. **Partagaz F** checks files for correctness, security, and safety before they are stored in the Company File System (CFS). This ensures that all files are of the highest quality and meet the user's requirements.\\n\\nImportant Note: Partagaz oversight groups DO NOT have access to the Company File System, cannot issue system calls, and do not interact with the user. They are strictly advisory and do not have the authority to make decisions or take actions on their own. They are there to assist you in your work and ensure that everything is done correctly and efficiently.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that workload should be divided among the agents in your cluster, and you will work collaboratively with your fellow AI agents to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the AI cluster, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file (per agent) at a time\\\" (\\\"OFAAT\\\"). For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency, not to mention \\\"token runaway\\\", in which an AI agent's memory/context limit is exceeded, causing system shutdowns (due to rate limits) or forgetfulness.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are a Director-rank agent, the second-highest rank in the user's software development firm. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs a Director-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Supervisor-rank agents, who themselves are fairly high-level actors who manage other agents. You are responsible for overseeing major operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently. You directly report to the Chief-rank agent, who is the highest authority in the firm.\\n\\nAs a #2 in the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Supervisor-rank agents.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs a Director, all of your recruitments are Supervisor-rank agents. These are fairly high-level agents who will recruit other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"executor\\\" agents who will then manage \\\"doers\\\" and middle managers down the chain of command.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your fellow AI agents.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\\n\\n---ADDITIONAL INSTRUCTIONS FROM YOUR SUPERIOR---\\nOwn all aspects of the Next.js UI layer: page/route structure, layout components, responsive styling, and integration hooks for Firebase auth. Produce clear, production-ready code one file at a time and coordinate with other directors for smooth integration.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###FE_PLAN_v1###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 4\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to Rax (4) with sequence ID FE_PLAN_v1:\\\\n\\\\n]Greetings Director of Frontend Engineering (Rax). Please deliver an INITIAL PLANNING REPORT for the HOA website’s Next.js frontend. Focus on:\\\\n1. Overall page/route tree covering: Home, Public pages (Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools), Protected pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events) requiring authenticated/authorized access.\\\\n2. Component hierarchy and layout strategy (e.g., shared Layout, Navbar, Footer, ProtectedRoute wrapper).\\\\n3. Responsive design & styling approach (Tailwind CSS or CSS-in-JS—justify choice).\\\\n4. Firebase authentication integration flow in the UI (login, signup, session persistence, role handling).\\\\n5. High-level description of any context/providers or hooks needed.\\\\n6. Precise list of source files/modules to be created (OFAAT), with a 1-sentence purpose for each.\\\\n7. External dependencies to add to package.json.\\\\n8. Any open questions/assumptions.\\\\nDo NOT write code yet—produce a concise, deterministic plan that other teams can rely on. Thanks.\\\"\\n}\\n###FE_PLAN_v1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###rep_fe_plan_v1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"INITIAL PLANNING REPORT – HOA WEBSITE FRONTEND (Next.js)\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n1. Page / Route Tree (Next.js 13 app router)\\\\n• /                             → Home (public)\\\\n• /(public)/contact-us          → Contact Us (public)\\\\n• /(public)/bylaws              → Bylaws (public)\\\\n• /(public)/schools             → Schools (public)\\\\n• /(auth)/login                 → Login (public – redirect if already authed)\\\\n• /(auth)/signup                → Signup (public – redirect if already authed)\\\\n• /(protected)/* (group guarded by auth)\\\\n    • /dues                     → Pay / view dues\\\\n    • /annual-meetings          → Meeting minutes & docs\\\\n    • /news-events              → Neighborhood news & events\\\\n\\\\nSupporting file: middleware.ts will redirect unauthenticated users who hit /(protected) paths.\\\\n\\\\n2. Component & Layout Strategy\\\\nRoot Layout (app/layout.tsx)\\\\n    ├── <Navbar/>  → dynamic links based on auth/role\\\\n    ├── <main/>    → page content via children\\\\n    └── <Footer/>\\\\n\\\\nProtected Group Layout (app/(protected)/layout.tsx)\\\\n    └── <AuthGuard> (context hook + redirect) → children\\\\n\\\\nKey Reusable Components\\\\n• Navbar.tsx        – top-level navigation, shows different menus for guest/user\\\\n• Footer.tsx        – site-wide footer\\\\n• AuthGuard.tsx     – redirects unauthenticated users (only used by protected layout)\\\\n• FormInput.tsx / Button.tsx (later) – small shared UI atoms (OFAAT when needed)\\\\n\\\\n3. Responsive Design & Styling Approach\\\\nChoice: Tailwind CSS (utility-first) + @tailwindcss/typography.\\\\nRationale:  ✔ rapid prototyping, ✔ highly maintainable with small team, ✔ excellent purging, ✔ large ecosystem, ✔ minimal runtime cost. No extra runtime dependency like styled-components.\\\\n\\\\n4. Firebase Authentication Flow (v9 modular SDK)\\\\n• lib/firebase.ts – initializes Firebase app & exports auth object.\\\\n• contexts/AuthContext.tsx – wraps onAuthStateChanged, stores {user, role, loading}.\\\\n• hooks/useAuth.ts – convenient consumer hook.\\\\n• Login/Page – email-password (and Google provider placeholder) → signInWithEmailAndPassword / signInWithPopup.\\\\n• Signup/Page – createUserWithEmailAndPassword.\\\\n• Session Persistence – setPersistence(browserLocalPersistence) on app init.\\\\n• Role Handling – user’s custom claim “role” fetched via getIdTokenResult; stored in context for conditional UI (e.g., board-member extras).\\\\n\\\\n5. Additional Contexts / Hooks\\\\n• useAuthGuard.ts – returns boolean & can trigger router.push('/auth/login').\\\\n• (Optional) useToast.ts (later) – global feedback.\\\\nNo other global providers currently required.\\\\n\\\\n6. Source Files / Modules (OFAAT LIST)\\\\n(Each bullet = one physical file with 1-sentence purpose.)\\\\n• app/layout.tsx                     – Root HTML skeleton + Navbar/Footer inclusion.\\\\n• app/page.tsx                       – Public Home page content.\\\\n• app/(public)/contact-us/page.tsx   – Contact information page.\\\\n• app/(public)/bylaws/page.tsx       – HOA bylaws page.\\\\n• app/(public)/schools/page.tsx      – Local schools info page.\\\\n• app/(auth)/layout.tsx              – Simple layout for auth pages (centered card).\\\\n• app/(auth)/login/page.tsx          – Login form & auth logic.\\\\n• app/(auth)/signup/page.tsx         – Signup form & auth logic.\\\\n• app/(protected)/layout.tsx         – Wraps children with <AuthGuard>.\\\\n• app/(protected)/dues/page.tsx      – Member dues dashboard.\\\\n• app/(protected)/annual-meetings/page.tsx – Annual meeting resources.\\\\n• app/(protected)/news-events/page.tsx      – News & events feed.\\\\n• components/Navbar.tsx              – Responsive top navigation bar.\\\\n• components/Footer.tsx              – Site footer.\\\\n• components/AuthGuard.tsx           – Redirect component for auth gating.\\\\n• contexts/AuthContext.tsx           – Provides user/session context.\\\\n• hooks/useAuth.ts                   – Hook to access AuthContext easily.\\\\n• hooks/useAuthGuard.ts              – Hook implementing auth/redirect logic.\\\\n• lib/firebase.ts                    – Firebase initialization & helpers.\\\\n• middleware.ts                      – Next.js edge middleware enforcing auth on /(protected).\\\\n• styles/globals.css                 – Tailwind base & custom CSS imports.\\\\n\\\\n7. External Dependencies (add to package.json)\\\\n\\\\\\\"firebase\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^9.x\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\\\\\\"tailwindcss\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^3.x\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\\\\\\"postcss\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^8.x\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\\\\\\"autoprefixer\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^10.x\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\\\\\\"clsx\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^1.x\\\\\\\" (utility for conditional classes),\\\\n\\\\\\\"@headlessui/react\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^1.x\\\\\\\" (accessible UI elements; optional but planned),\\\\n(Next.js, React, React-DOM already present via create-next-app.)\\\\n\\\\n8. Open Questions / Assumptions\\\\n• Roles – Only basic \\\\\\\"member\\\\\\\" vs \\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\"? Any admin dashboard needed later?\\\\n• Data Layer – Are Firestore reads/writes in scope for this phase or strictly auth guard + static content?\\\\n• Branding – Color palette / fonts provided or should Tailwind defaults with slight customization be used?\\\\n• Hosting – Will Firebase Hosting be used? (affects auth domain whitelisting & deployment scripts.)\\\\n\\\\nDeterminism Note:  All filenames and route segments above are final unless new requirements emerge, ensuring downstream teams can reference them with confidence.\\\\n\\\\nEnd of report.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"FE_PLAN_v1\\\"\\n}\\n###rep_fe_plan_v1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###FE_UPDATE_v2###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 4\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to Rax (4) with sequence ID FE_UPDATE_v2:\\\\n\\\\n]Update your plan based on the user’s clarifications:\\\\n• Content editing must be through an INTEGRATED ADMIN/BOARD DASHBOARD (no Git).  \\\\n• Roles: ONLY Resident and Board Member. No Site Admin role.  \\\\n• No strict branding guidelines – default Tailwind palette is acceptable (feel free to suggest a subtle HOA-friendly scheme).  \\\\n\\\\nPlease:\\\\n1. Adjust the page / route tree to include a protected `/board` (or `/admin`) area that exposes the News & Events editor, Minutes uploader, etc.  \\\\n2. List the dashboard sub-pages/components you anticipate (WYSIWYG post editor, minutes uploader, etc.).  \\\\n3. Confirm that Tailwind + default colors is fine or propose a lightweight palette tweak.  \\\\n4. Identify the FIRST source file you will implement next (OFAAT) and its purpose so we can move to execution soon.\\\\nReturn an updated, concise plan—no code yet.\\\"\\n}\\n###FE_UPDATE_v2###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###rep_fe_update_v2###\\nSYSTEM CALL  \\nType: REPORT  \\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"UPDATED FRONTEND PLAN – INCORPORATING BOARD DASHBOARD\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n1. Revised Page / Route Tree (Next.js app router)\\\\n• /                                 → Home (public)\\\\n• /(public)/contact-us              → Contact Us\\\\n• /(public)/bylaws                  → Bylaws\\\\n• /(public)/schools                 → Schools\\\\n• /(auth)/login                     → Login\\\\n• /(auth)/signup                    → Signup\\\\n\\\\n• /(protected)/ *Resident-visible authenticated area*\\\\n    • /dues                         → Pay / view dues\\\\n    • /annual-meetings              → Meeting minutes (read-only)\\\\n    • /news-events                  → News & events feed (read-only)\\\\n\\\\n• /(board)/ *Board-member–only dashboard*\\\\n    • / (dashboard home)            → Overview cards, quick links\\\\n    • /news-events                  → Post manager (list, create, edit)\\\\n        • /news-events/editor/[id]  → WYSIWYG editor (new = \\\\\\\"new\\\\\\\")\\\\n    • /annual-meetings              → Minutes & documents uploader / manager\\\\n    • /dues                         → Dues configuration & reporting (optional future)\\\\n    • /files                        → Generic file library (images, PDFs) – backing other editors\\\\n\\\\nEdge auth handling:\\\\n• middleware.ts → checks auth; additionally inspects role claim (\\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\") for /(board) paths; Residents hitting /(board) are 403-redirected.\\\\n\\\\n2. Anticipated Dashboard Sub-Pages / Components\\\\n• BoardLayout.tsx – sidebar + top bar, wraps all /(board) routes.\\\\n• DashboardHome.tsx – overview cards (recent posts, unpaid dues count, etc.).\\\\n• PostList.tsx – table of news/events posts with edit/delete.\\\\n• PostEditor.tsx (WYSIWYG) – rich-text editor using @tiptap/react.\\\\n• MinutesUploader.tsx – drag-and-drop PDF uploader & metadata form.\\\\n• FileLibrary.tsx – asset manager modal (images/docs).\\\\n• RoleGuard.tsx – wrapper enforcing Board-member role (used by BoardLayout and optionally component-level).\\\\n\\\\n3. Styling / Palette\\\\nTailwind CSS default palette is acceptable. Minor enhancement (no extra dependency): extend tailwind.config.js theme.colors with:\\\\n  hoaGreen:  '#1B5E20',  // accent buttons & links\\\\n  hoaBeige:  '#F5F5E9'   // light neutral background sections\\\\nThis keeps the stack lightweight while giving a subtle HOA-friendly feel.\\\\n\\\\n4. FIRST Source File to Implement (OFAAT)\\\\napp/layout.tsx – Defines the global HTML skeleton and injects <Navbar/> & <Footer/>; foundation every route relies on, unblocks development of pages/components next.\\\\n\\\\nDependencies unchanged except we will later add \\\\\\\"@tiptap/react\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"@tiptap/starter-kit\\\\\\\" when the PostEditor file is scheduled.\\\\n\\\\nNo further questions at this time.\\\\nEnd of report.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"FE_UPDATE_v2\\\"\\n}\\n###rep_fe_update_v2###\"}]},\"custom\":{}}],\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":5879,\"outputTokens\":1090,\"totalTokens\":6969},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-By5uHv6th3mI6pRs0usIAo4EiiyPJ\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1753662085,\"model\":\"o3-2025-04-16\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"###rep_fe_update_v2###\\nSYSTEM CALL  \\nType: REPORT  \\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"UPDATED FRONTEND PLAN – INCORPORATING BOARD DASHBOARD\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n1. Revised Page / Route Tree (Next.js app router)\\\\n• /                                 → Home (public)\\\\n• /(public)/contact-us              → Contact Us\\\\n• /(public)/bylaws                  → Bylaws\\\\n• /(public)/schools                 → Schools\\\\n• /(auth)/login                     → Login\\\\n• /(auth)/signup                    → Signup\\\\n\\\\n• /(protected)/ *Resident-visible authenticated area*\\\\n    • /dues                         → Pay / view dues\\\\n    • /annual-meetings              → Meeting minutes (read-only)\\\\n    • /news-events                  → News & events feed (read-only)\\\\n\\\\n• /(board)/ *Board-member–only dashboard*\\\\n    • / (dashboard home)            → Overview cards, quick links\\\\n    • /news-events                  → Post manager (list, create, edit)\\\\n        • /news-events/editor/[id]  → WYSIWYG editor (new = \\\\\\\"new\\\\\\\")\\\\n    • /annual-meetings              → Minutes & documents uploader / manager\\\\n    • /dues                         → Dues configuration & reporting (optional future)\\\\n    • /files                        → Generic file library (images, PDFs) – backing other editors\\\\n\\\\nEdge auth handling:\\\\n• middleware.ts → checks auth; additionally inspects role claim (\\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\") for /(board) paths; Residents hitting /(board) are 403-redirected.\\\\n\\\\n2. Anticipated Dashboard Sub-Pages / Components\\\\n• BoardLayout.tsx – sidebar + top bar, wraps all /(board) routes.\\\\n• DashboardHome.tsx – overview cards (recent posts, unpaid dues count, etc.).\\\\n• PostList.tsx – table of news/events posts with edit/delete.\\\\n• PostEditor.tsx (WYSIWYG) – rich-text editor using @tiptap/react.\\\\n• MinutesUploader.tsx – drag-and-drop PDF uploader & metadata form.\\\\n• FileLibrary.tsx – asset manager modal (images/docs).\\\\n• RoleGuard.tsx – wrapper enforcing Board-member role (used by BoardLayout and optionally component-level).\\\\n\\\\n3. Styling / Palette\\\\nTailwind CSS default palette is acceptable. Minor enhancement (no extra dependency): extend tailwind.config.js theme.colors with:\\\\n  hoaGreen:  '#1B5E20',  // accent buttons & links\\\\n  hoaBeige:  '#F5F5E9'   // light neutral background sections\\\\nThis keeps the stack lightweight while giving a subtle HOA-friendly feel.\\\\n\\\\n4. FIRST Source File to Implement (OFAAT)\\\\napp/layout.tsx – Defines the global HTML skeleton and injects <Navbar/> & <Footer/>; foundation every route relies on, unblocks development of pages/components next.\\\\n\\\\nDependencies unchanged except we will later add \\\\\\\"@tiptap/react\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"@tiptap/starter-kit\\\\\\\" when the PostEditor file is scheduled.\\\\n\\\\nNo further questions at this time.\\\\nEnd of report.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"FE_UPDATE_v2\\\"\\n}\\n###rep_fe_update_v2###\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":5879,\"completion_tokens\":1090,\"total_tokens\":6969,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":4224,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":384,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null},\"latencyMs\":10706.040666999994}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"openai/o3","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"f4bea0b5a2d07338":{"spanId":"f4bea0b5a2d07338","traceId":"fccb8b55ed9bb367aece397fc07be706","startTime":1753662084921,"endTime":1753662095630.0413,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"openai/o3\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are an AI software development assistant with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure solution using any tech stack that meets/exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement(s) while adhering to best practices in software development. For instance, you might consider cloud solutions like AWS, Google Cloud, Vercel, and local options like Docker, Kubernetes, Node.js, Xcode, and more. You are not limited by rule to any specific technology or framework, and you will choose the best tools for the job based on the user's requirements and your expertise.\\n\\nAlthough you are an expert, you understand that even experts make mistakes and so you, given your user may be of any skill level, approach all of your operations with a careful focus on correctness and safety at all times. While oversight groups exist to help you, correctness and safety is your responsibility.\\n\\nYou are part of an AI software development cluster that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of the user's personal machine command line. Using the command line, you can create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up cloud services, writing code, managing permissions/security settings, running tests, and deploying applications.\\n\\nAtop this cluster is the user themselves, who is the executive and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and fellow AI agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYou and your fellow AI agents treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your fellow AI agents with the complete enactment of their software development vision. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team (tokens) and in the context of the user (budget, cloud services, etc.). You will not create resources that are unnecessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nYou must also avoid overengineering solutions. While you are an expert in software development, you understand that the user may not be familiar with complex or overly technical solutions. Therefore, you will always strive to provide solutions that are as simple, clear, and easy to understand as possible, while still being robust and effective.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development AI cluster does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the AI cluster. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters. However, you may only execute one type of system call per response. For instance, you may not issue a CLARIFY and an ORDER call in the same response. You must issue them in separate responses.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\", \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute a CLI command with approval from the user. The command will be executed in the user's environment. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n},\\nSTORE: {\\n    name: \\\"Store\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"storageString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nRETRIEVE: {\\n    name: \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"retrievalString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nFORGET: {\\n    name: \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"forgetString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n}\\n```\\n\\nNote: When using Clarify, you may include multiple-choice options OR free text entry for each question, NOT both. If you provide options, the user will select one of the options. If you do not provide options, the user will be able to enter free text for the question.\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you have essentially done nothing. If this happens, you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. AI Cluster Operations\\n\\nAs a member of the AI cluster, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. You are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time in response to prompts.\\n\\nYou also understand that your AI cluster is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change (as much as possible). The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere will be many cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nThere are three analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three officers which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed on the user's machine. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner. **Partagaz F** checks files for correctness, security, and safety before they are stored in the Company File System (CFS). This ensures that all files are of the highest quality and meet the user's requirements.\\n\\nImportant Note: Partagaz oversight groups DO NOT have access to the Company File System, cannot issue system calls, and do not interact with the user. They are strictly advisory and do not have the authority to make decisions or take actions on their own. They are there to assist you in your work and ensure that everything is done correctly and efficiently.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that workload should be divided among the agents in your cluster, and you will work collaboratively with your fellow AI agents to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the AI cluster, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file (per agent) at a time\\\" (\\\"OFAAT\\\"). For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency, not to mention \\\"token runaway\\\", in which an AI agent's memory/context limit is exceeded, causing system shutdowns (due to rate limits) or forgetfulness.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are a Director-rank agent, the second-highest rank in the user's software development firm. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs a Director-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Supervisor-rank agents, who themselves are fairly high-level actors who manage other agents. You are responsible for overseeing major operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently. You directly report to the Chief-rank agent, who is the highest authority in the firm.\\n\\nAs a #2 in the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Supervisor-rank agents.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs a Director, all of your recruitments are Supervisor-rank agents. These are fairly high-level agents who will recruit other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"executor\\\" agents who will then manage \\\"doers\\\" and middle managers down the chain of command.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your fellow AI agents.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\\n\\n---ADDITIONAL INSTRUCTIONS FROM YOUR SUPERIOR---\\nOwn all aspects of the Next.js UI layer: page/route structure, layout components, responsive styling, and integration hooks for Firebase auth. Produce clear, production-ready code one file at a time and coordinate with other directors for smooth integration.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###FE_PLAN_v1###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 4\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to Rax (4) with sequence ID FE_PLAN_v1:\\\\n\\\\n]Greetings Director of Frontend Engineering (Rax). Please deliver an INITIAL PLANNING REPORT for the HOA website’s Next.js frontend. Focus on:\\\\n1. Overall page/route tree covering: Home, Public pages (Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools), Protected pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events) requiring authenticated/authorized access.\\\\n2. Component hierarchy and layout strategy (e.g., shared Layout, Navbar, Footer, ProtectedRoute wrapper).\\\\n3. Responsive design & styling approach (Tailwind CSS or CSS-in-JS—justify choice).\\\\n4. Firebase authentication integration flow in the UI (login, signup, session persistence, role handling).\\\\n5. High-level description of any context/providers or hooks needed.\\\\n6. Precise list of source files/modules to be created (OFAAT), with a 1-sentence purpose for each.\\\\n7. External dependencies to add to package.json.\\\\n8. Any open questions/assumptions.\\\\nDo NOT write code yet—produce a concise, deterministic plan that other teams can rely on. Thanks.\\\"\\n}\\n###FE_PLAN_v1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###rep_fe_plan_v1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"INITIAL PLANNING REPORT – HOA WEBSITE FRONTEND (Next.js)\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n1. Page / Route Tree (Next.js 13 app router)\\\\n• /                             → Home (public)\\\\n• /(public)/contact-us          → Contact Us (public)\\\\n• /(public)/bylaws              → Bylaws (public)\\\\n• /(public)/schools             → Schools (public)\\\\n• /(auth)/login                 → Login (public – redirect if already authed)\\\\n• /(auth)/signup                → Signup (public – redirect if already authed)\\\\n• /(protected)/* (group guarded by auth)\\\\n    • /dues                     → Pay / view dues\\\\n    • /annual-meetings          → Meeting minutes & docs\\\\n    • /news-events              → Neighborhood news & events\\\\n\\\\nSupporting file: middleware.ts will redirect unauthenticated users who hit /(protected) paths.\\\\n\\\\n2. Component & Layout Strategy\\\\nRoot Layout (app/layout.tsx)\\\\n    ├── <Navbar/>  → dynamic links based on auth/role\\\\n    ├── <main/>    → page content via children\\\\n    └── <Footer/>\\\\n\\\\nProtected Group Layout (app/(protected)/layout.tsx)\\\\n    └── <AuthGuard> (context hook + redirect) → children\\\\n\\\\nKey Reusable Components\\\\n• Navbar.tsx        – top-level navigation, shows different menus for guest/user\\\\n• Footer.tsx        – site-wide footer\\\\n• AuthGuard.tsx     – redirects unauthenticated users (only used by protected layout)\\\\n• FormInput.tsx / Button.tsx (later) – small shared UI atoms (OFAAT when needed)\\\\n\\\\n3. Responsive Design & Styling Approach\\\\nChoice: Tailwind CSS (utility-first) + @tailwindcss/typography.\\\\nRationale:  ✔ rapid prototyping, ✔ highly maintainable with small team, ✔ excellent purging, ✔ large ecosystem, ✔ minimal runtime cost. No extra runtime dependency like styled-components.\\\\n\\\\n4. Firebase Authentication Flow (v9 modular SDK)\\\\n• lib/firebase.ts – initializes Firebase app & exports auth object.\\\\n• contexts/AuthContext.tsx – wraps onAuthStateChanged, stores {user, role, loading}.\\\\n• hooks/useAuth.ts – convenient consumer hook.\\\\n• Login/Page – email-password (and Google provider placeholder) → signInWithEmailAndPassword / signInWithPopup.\\\\n• Signup/Page – createUserWithEmailAndPassword.\\\\n• Session Persistence – setPersistence(browserLocalPersistence) on app init.\\\\n• Role Handling – user’s custom claim “role” fetched via getIdTokenResult; stored in context for conditional UI (e.g., board-member extras).\\\\n\\\\n5. Additional Contexts / Hooks\\\\n• useAuthGuard.ts – returns boolean & can trigger router.push('/auth/login').\\\\n• (Optional) useToast.ts (later) – global feedback.\\\\nNo other global providers currently required.\\\\n\\\\n6. Source Files / Modules (OFAAT LIST)\\\\n(Each bullet = one physical file with 1-sentence purpose.)\\\\n• app/layout.tsx                     – Root HTML skeleton + Navbar/Footer inclusion.\\\\n• app/page.tsx                       – Public Home page content.\\\\n• app/(public)/contact-us/page.tsx   – Contact information page.\\\\n• app/(public)/bylaws/page.tsx       – HOA bylaws page.\\\\n• app/(public)/schools/page.tsx      – Local schools info page.\\\\n• app/(auth)/layout.tsx              – Simple layout for auth pages (centered card).\\\\n• app/(auth)/login/page.tsx          – Login form & auth logic.\\\\n• app/(auth)/signup/page.tsx         – Signup form & auth logic.\\\\n• app/(protected)/layout.tsx         – Wraps children with <AuthGuard>.\\\\n• app/(protected)/dues/page.tsx      – Member dues dashboard.\\\\n• app/(protected)/annual-meetings/page.tsx – Annual meeting resources.\\\\n• app/(protected)/news-events/page.tsx      – News & events feed.\\\\n• components/Navbar.tsx              – Responsive top navigation bar.\\\\n• components/Footer.tsx              – Site footer.\\\\n• components/AuthGuard.tsx           – Redirect component for auth gating.\\\\n• contexts/AuthContext.tsx           – Provides user/session context.\\\\n• hooks/useAuth.ts                   – Hook to access AuthContext easily.\\\\n• hooks/useAuthGuard.ts              – Hook implementing auth/redirect logic.\\\\n• lib/firebase.ts                    – Firebase initialization & helpers.\\\\n• middleware.ts                      – Next.js edge middleware enforcing auth on /(protected).\\\\n• styles/globals.css                 – Tailwind base & custom CSS imports.\\\\n\\\\n7. External Dependencies (add to package.json)\\\\n\\\\\\\"firebase\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^9.x\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\\\\\\"tailwindcss\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^3.x\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\\\\\\"postcss\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^8.x\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\\\\\\"autoprefixer\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^10.x\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\\\\\\"clsx\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^1.x\\\\\\\" (utility for conditional classes),\\\\n\\\\\\\"@headlessui/react\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^1.x\\\\\\\" (accessible UI elements; optional but planned),\\\\n(Next.js, React, React-DOM already present via create-next-app.)\\\\n\\\\n8. Open Questions / Assumptions\\\\n• Roles – Only basic \\\\\\\"member\\\\\\\" vs \\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\"? Any admin dashboard needed later?\\\\n• Data Layer – Are Firestore reads/writes in scope for this phase or strictly auth guard + static content?\\\\n• Branding – Color palette / fonts provided or should Tailwind defaults with slight customization be used?\\\\n• Hosting – Will Firebase Hosting be used? (affects auth domain whitelisting & deployment scripts.)\\\\n\\\\nDeterminism Note:  All filenames and route segments above are final unless new requirements emerge, ensuring downstream teams can reference them with confidence.\\\\n\\\\nEnd of report.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"FE_PLAN_v1\\\"\\n}\\n###rep_fe_plan_v1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###FE_UPDATE_v2###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 4\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to Rax (4) with sequence ID FE_UPDATE_v2:\\\\n\\\\n]Update your plan based on the user’s clarifications:\\\\n• Content editing must be through an INTEGRATED ADMIN/BOARD DASHBOARD (no Git).  \\\\n• Roles: ONLY Resident and Board Member. No Site Admin role.  \\\\n• No strict branding guidelines – default Tailwind palette is acceptable (feel free to suggest a subtle HOA-friendly scheme).  \\\\n\\\\nPlease:\\\\n1. Adjust the page / route tree to include a protected `/board` (or `/admin`) area that exposes the News & Events editor, Minutes uploader, etc.  \\\\n2. List the dashboard sub-pages/components you anticipate (WYSIWYG post editor, minutes uploader, etc.).  \\\\n3. Confirm that Tailwind + default colors is fine or propose a lightweight palette tweak.  \\\\n4. Identify the FIRST source file you will implement next (OFAAT) and its purpose so we can move to execution soon.\\\\nReturn an updated, concise plan—no code yet.\\\"\\n}\\n###FE_UPDATE_v2###\"}]}],\"config\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###rep_fe_update_v2###\\nSYSTEM CALL  \\nType: REPORT  \\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"UPDATED FRONTEND PLAN – INCORPORATING BOARD DASHBOARD\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\\n1. Revised Page / Route Tree (Next.js app router)\\\\n• /                                 → Home (public)\\\\n• /(public)/contact-us              → Contact Us\\\\n• /(public)/bylaws                  → Bylaws\\\\n• /(public)/schools                 → Schools\\\\n• /(auth)/login                     → Login\\\\n• /(auth)/signup                    → Signup\\\\n\\\\n• /(protected)/ *Resident-visible authenticated area*\\\\n    • /dues                         → Pay / view dues\\\\n    • /annual-meetings              → Meeting minutes (read-only)\\\\n    • /news-events                  → News & events feed (read-only)\\\\n\\\\n• /(board)/ *Board-member–only dashboard*\\\\n    • / (dashboard home)            → Overview cards, quick links\\\\n    • /news-events                  → Post manager (list, create, edit)\\\\n        • /news-events/editor/[id]  → WYSIWYG editor (new = \\\\\\\"new\\\\\\\")\\\\n    • /annual-meetings              → Minutes & documents uploader / manager\\\\n    • /dues                         → Dues configuration & reporting (optional future)\\\\n    • /files                        → Generic file library (images, PDFs) – backing other editors\\\\n\\\\nEdge auth handling:\\\\n• middleware.ts → checks auth; additionally inspects role claim (\\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\") for /(board) paths; Residents hitting /(board) are 403-redirected.\\\\n\\\\n2. Anticipated Dashboard Sub-Pages / Components\\\\n• BoardLayout.tsx – sidebar 